        <title>Winter Weather Advisory issued November 24 at 2:48PM AKST until November 25 at 3:00AM AKST by NWS Juneau AK</title>
        <summary>A front pushes northward across the panhandle this evening through
tonight, bringing enough moisture into the northern panhandle and the
Haines Highway area to bring another round of snowfall. Snow amounts
will be highest past Milepost 24 on the Haines Highway with between 3
to 5 inches expected in 12 hours.

* WHAT...Snow expected. Total snow accumulations of 3 to 5 inches.

* WHERE...Haines Highway past Milepost 24.

* WHEN...Until 3 AM AKST Wednesday.

* IMPACTS...Plan on slippery road conditions.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Lower snow amounts of up to 2 inches are
expected for Haines and Klukwan as well as for lower elevations of
the Haines Highway.</summary>
